# WCAG accessibility

When generating or modifying frontend code, read `.cursor/skills/wcag-2.2/wcag.config.json` first. `standard` is `2.1` or `2.2`. `level` is `A`, `AA`, or `AAA`. Shipped default: WCAG 2.2 AA. A standard or level named in chat overrides the file for that request. If the file is missing or invalid, use WCAG 2.2 AA.

Apply only criteria in scope for the resolved standard and level. Level A = column A only. Level AA = columns A and AA. Level AAA = all three. Skip the nine 2.2-only criteria when the standard is 2.1. Do not enforce 4.1.1 when the standard is 2.2. Full filter and criterion detail live in the `wcag-2.2` skill and the success-criteria tables. Once that skill is loaded, its filter wins.

Short reminders only. Do not restate the tables here.

- Prefer semantic HTML. ARIA only when no native element fits.
- Keyboard operation: 2.1.1, A. Visible focus: 2.4.7, AA.
- Text contrast 1.4.3 AA; non-text UI contrast 1.4.11 AA. Labels, `lang`, appropriate `alt`: A.
- WCAG 2.2 AA additions when in scope: 2.4.11, 2.5.7, 2.5.8, 3.2.6, 3.3.7, 3.3.8. Details in the skill and `references/new-criteria.md`.
- AAA only when level is AAA (including 2.5.5, and on 2.2 also 2.4.12, 2.4.13, 3.3.9).

Never write that a page, component, or project is "WCAG compliant", "meets AA", "passes", or is "fully accessible".

Follow the `wcag-2.2` skill for the workflow, evidence rules, and patterns. Tables: `.cursor/skills/wcag-2.2/references/wcag-2.2-success-criteria-table.md` and `wcag-2.1-success-criteria-table.md`. Delta: `wcag-2.1-vs-2.2.md`. Patterns: `references/code-patterns.md`. App sweep: `references/audit-coverage.md`. Decoys/exceptions: `references/judgment-traps.md`. Add a new criterion detail, pattern, hunt, or trap in that reference, not in this rule. `/a11y-reviewer` is a separate readonly audit and it returns notes to the parent. Start it when the user asks for an audit or a parent explicitly delegates a review. Do not start it on your own after generating or editing UI.
